Campfire wasm patch 0105: re-key a copy of a wallet database ("Export wallet.db").

The web app keeps each created or restored wallet.db under a random 64-hex
database password (sealed in envelopes), which the person never sees. To hand
out a wallet.db that BEAM's desktop wallet, Campfire desktop or the CLI can
open, the app copies wallet.db into memory and re-keys THAT COPY to a password
the person knows; the live wallet.db is never touched.

The wallet API's change_password re-keys only the live database of a running
wallet, so this adds a static WasmWalletClient.RekeyFile(path, oldPass,
newPass, cb): on an engine thread (like CheckPassword) it opens the file with
the old key, proves it reads, sqlite3_rekey()s it, closes it, reopens it
read-only with the new key to prove the result, and calls cb(ok) on the main
thread. Neither password is logged. wallet_core links sqlite privately and
sqlite3.h hides sqlite3_key/sqlite3_rekey without SQLITE_HAS_CODEC, so the
two are declared explicitly.

--- a/wasmclient/wasmclient.cpp
+++ b/wasmclient/wasmclient.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,14 @@
